# What must never enter an image build context.
#
# ===========================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND THE FAILURE THAT PRODUCED IT
# ===========================================================================
# `Dockerfile.twinsim` does `COPY lab ./lab` and `Dockerfile.service` does
# `COPY core ./core` / `COPY services ./services`. Without this file those copy
# the `target/` directories too, and three things follow:
#
#   1. THE BUILD IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE. ADR-0018 §11.10 BM-6 remaps source paths
#      and pins SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH so the artifact is a function of the source.
#      A build context carrying one machine's `target/` makes it a function of
#      that machine's build history instead.
#   2. IT IS ENORMOUS. `lab/target` alone is hundreds of megabytes of rlibs
#      that `cargo build --locked --offline` immediately ignores.
#   3. IT RACES. Observed: `COPY lab ./lab` failed with
#      `lstat /lab/target/debug/deps/libtwinnet-*.rlib: no such file or
#      directory` because a concurrent `cargo` replaced the file between the
#      copier's stat and its read. A build that fails when somebody else is
#      compiling is a build nobody can trust.
#
# Everything below is either regenerated by the build or must not be in an
# image at all.

# Rust build output. `cargo fetch --locked` and `cargo build --offline` need the
# manifests and the lockfiles, never the artifacts.
target/
**/target/

# ===========================================================================
# KEY MATERIAL. Never, under any circumstances.
# ===========================================================================
# `infra/secrets/` holds development TLS keys, relay static Noise keys and the
# development issuer's SIGNING SEED. None of it belongs in an image layer --
# a layer is world-readable to anyone who can pull the image, and a deleted
# file in a later layer is still in the earlier one.
infra/secrets/
.env
.env.*

# Source control and tooling state.
.git/
.github/
node_modules/
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.swarm/
*.db

# Local run state.
**/*.log
**/*.pid
